            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Radon+measure"} Radon measure
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
            is
            = succeed "-additive." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi τ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
          %ul
            %li
              the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+measures"} Dirac measures
            %li
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lebesgue+measure"} Lebesgue measure
              on the real line,
            %li
              the measure induced by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume+form"} volume form
              of a Riemannian manifold,
            %li
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haar+measure"} Haar measure
              on a Lie group (or more generally a locally compact Hausdorff topological group).
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#pushforward_products_and_marginals Pushforward, products and marginals
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushforward+measure"} pushforward measure
                of a
                = succeed "-additive" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi τ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
                is itself
                = succeed "-additive." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi τ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/marginals"} marginals
                of a
                = succeed "-additive" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi τ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
                = succeed "-additive." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi τ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
                (see
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#monad_structure"} below
            %li
              %p
                The
                %span.newWikiWord
                  product
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/product+measure"} ?
                of two
                = succeed "-additive" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi τ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
                = succeed "-additive" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi τ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
          %h3#monad_structure Monad structure
          %p
            One can form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure+monad"} measure monad
            analogous to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giry+monad"} Giry monad
            = succeed "-additive" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi τ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+probabilistic+powerdomain"} extended probabilistic powerdomain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+probabilistic+powerdomain#the_measure_monad_on_top"} the measure monad on Top
            for more details.
          %h3#null_sets_and_support Null sets and support
          %p
            Given a tau-additive measure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            on a topological space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\subseteq X
            is called
            %strong null
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            if
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu(U)=0
            %strong full measure
            if its complement is null.
          %p
            By
            = succeed "-additivity," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi τ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support"} support
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
          %p
            This definition can be extended to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valuation+%28measure+theory%29#null_sets_and_support"} continuous valuations
          %h3#relationship_with_other_measuretheoretical_notions Relationship with other measure-theoretical notions
          %ul
            %li
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Radon+measure"} Radon measure
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
              is
              = succeed "-additive." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi τ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
            %li
              Every
              = succeed "-additive" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi τ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+space"} compact Hausdorff space
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Radon+measure"} Radon
            %li
              Every
              = succeed "-additive" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi τ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+valuation"} continuous valuation
            %li
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+valuation"} continuous valuation
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+space"} regular
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
              or on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+space"} locally compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+space"} sober space
              can be extended to a
              = succeed "-additive" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi τ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
          %p
            See also:
